WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:13.520
That was probably one of the better years in my career as far as personal goals or personal stats or whatever.

2
00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:15.280
I remember carrying the football a lot.

3
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:19.120
I think I averaged about twenty-eight carries a game.

4
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.300
It was just . . . It was a great year.

5
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.440
The offensive line did a great job.

6
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.900
We had a two-quarterback system.

7
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:31.820
I remember one game in particular, [against] Rice [University] I only played a quarter and a half.

8
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:33.660
I had 150 yards.

9
00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:38.840
I remember Carlos Carson scoring five touchdowns in one game.

10
00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:45.440
We beat Rice seventy-seven to nothing and it was just . . . We really had a powerful offense that year.

11
00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:49.820
We would just line up and we had Carlos Carson on one end.

12
00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:51.840
We had Tracy Porter at a flanker.

13
00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:55.360
We had Leroy Jones; he was on that team.

14
00:00:55.360 --> 00:01:00.080
Let me see, Thad Minaldi, Kelly Simmons.

15
00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.680
We really had some explosive players in the backfield and in wide receiving and some real good quarterbacks.

16
00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.200
So, that was a great year.

17
00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:12.760
Do you have any thoughts about what happens to the mood of a team when it’s been going through a rough time,

18
00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:17.500
then all of a sudden it turns things around and has a good year?

19
00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:22.820
Well, you know winning and losing is contagious.

20
00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:28.940
If you get in a rut of losing all the time, it can spread and you can get used to it.

21
00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:33.320
On the other hand, if you’re winning, things are a lot better.

22
00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:35.040
It is contagious also.

23
00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:43.080
It was definitely much more fun . . . more fun around here my last two years than in my first two years.

24
00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.400
My last two years, we won eight games.

25
00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:49.400
Those were some good times and I’ll never forget them.
